From c8a026701bcff566fe6d523240d5967c1442aa71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:49:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 366/367] DOS-PORT: patch 0366 -- lever R1: an unchanged GUI
 that nothing touched this frame is not composited (DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP, default
 on)

Why: Maniac Mansion Deluxe in play drew about 2 frames in 3 on the 486 (round P9 67.6%) while its character
select held 99.9%. The difference was the render pass, not logic (dosags LAB-PLAY.md sections 2-3): three GUIs
(the verb bar 320x57 twice and a 320x16 strip, 41,280 masked pixels) were composited in full on every frame though
none of them changed. They were already on 0169/0191/0234's skip-invalidate list, and 0170's clip that would limit
them to the dirty region was opt-in and off. In DOSBox-X at fixed 40000 they were 4.9 of 5.4-6.5 ms of sprite
drawing per pass. Round GC (same-binary ABBA on the 486, lab exe): MMD in play 66.39 / 65.97% -> 88.72 / 89.30%
displayed; rb_sprite_time per drawn frame 7.97 -> 4.12 ms; AGS Quest AutoPilot 93.01 -> 97.09%.

What: 0170 clips an unchanged, idempotent entry to the frame's dirty bbox plus 0236's carry boxes, and drew it in
full when the entry's rect missed that region. A clip to an empty rect draws nothing, so such an entry is now not
composited at all: outside the region the buffer still holds this same composite from the last frame that drew it
(the restore, every room sprite and every non-skipped UI entry are inside the region; skipped UI entries are clipped
to it). DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP: unset (or any other value) = 2, this skip; 0 = off, every GUI composited in full as in the
0365 head; 1 = 0170+0236's clip without the skip.
Latch: a change of the back buffer (virtualScreen object, pixel base or size), an alias activate or deactivate, or
a tint or plugin entry forces full composition -- no clip, no skip, exactly mode 0's drawing -- for that frame and
the next. So does a whole-surface restore the dirty set was not told about, for the frame it repaints: AGS turns a
26th rect in one restore interval into WHOLESCREENDIRTY (invalidate_rect_on_surf) without telling dos_port_dirty, so
the bbox the clip reads would be smaller than what the restore repainted (found by the R3 lab, dosags LAB-R3.md; seen
3-18 times a run in MMD, the intro and AGS Quest). The room restore and the black fill check for it and arm the latch
(dos_guiclip_note_fullrestore).
Witness: "DOS-PORT guiclip DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP=<value|(default)> mode=<0|1|2>" once at startup, and in RUNMANI.LOG
"DOS-PORT guiclip_final mode= flagged= skipped= skipped_px= clipped= full= latched_full= latch_events=
latch_alias= latch_buffer= latch_tint= latch_fullrestore=" in both flavours. DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP joins the RUNMANIFEST env allowlist.

Gates (DOSBox-X, fixed 40000; LAB-PLAY.md 7 and 9): a per-frame digest of the composited virtual screen, every
tick rendered, default vs 0: EQUAL on every tick of MMD in play (save 007, clicks and hovers, 3164 ticks) and the
MMD intro (1299 ticks); a control that skips every flagged entry DIFFs (2443 / 781 ticks). Never engages on 5 Days
room 3 (its 320x200 picture sits in a 320x240 virtual screen, so 0170's same-space test fails) or Trilby room 35.

